    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\nI added email uniqueness enforcement mirroring the existing telephone-unique pattern, keeping structural impact minimal \u2014 all new small classes, plus a two-line wiring insert into the POST pipeline:\n\n- **`EnsureOwnerEmailUnique`** \u2014 a new single-method function (CC 2, no surrounding class complexity) that throws when the owner's email (already lower-cased by `Owner.setEmail`) matches any other owner's.\n- **`DuplicateEmailException`** \u2014 checked exception so it surfaces in the `throws` clause.\n- **`DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds **409 Conflict** with a `ProblemDetail`.\n- **`DuplicateEmailException.yml`** escalation mapping.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `ensureUniqueEmail` step (under `transaction` governance) between telephone and household checks.\n\nNo existing function bodies were grown; the only edit to an existing file is the YAML wiring. The `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` acceptance test and the full suite pass.",
